The demand for faster publishing schedules and higher typographic
precision has fundamentally reshaped scholarly publishing workflows.
While traditional word-processing tools struggle to meet these rigorous
expectations\Dash often leading to formatting inconsistencies and manual
delays\Dash \TeX\ and \XML-based workflows offer a robust solution. \TeX\
ensures absolute typographic accuracy and mathematical elegance, while
\XML\ provides structured, machine-readable data essential for
multi-channel digital publishing. This paper explores the evolving
pressures placed on typesetters, analyzes the challenges of handling
complex author-supplied files, and presents specialized software
solutions\Dash specifically \textsf{Neptune} (\TeX-based) and
\textsf{Primo} (\XML-based)\Dash developed to harmonize author expectations
with publisher requirements.
